    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Lang Ya land spirit hands Fang Yuan a Bookworm emanating rank three aura. Fang Yuan has seen Bookworms before as valuable rank one Gu. Lang Ya’s previous self broke the limits of the rank one Bookworm and developed rank two and rank three versions. Fang Yuan does not own this copy. He borrows it from Lang Ya land spirit and reads three true inheritances stored inside.",
        "chapters": [
          1051
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-two-and-three",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
          "fac_lang_ya_sect"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is like a silkworm. It has a head, body, and stomach as three distinct parts, yet overall it looks like a cocoon, round and cute. The body is white, with a layer of enamel on the surface that gives an oily glow. Held in the hand it is round and smooth, like a high grade porcelain vase.",
        "chapters": [
          261
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It is a storage type Gu. The Tusita flower stores physical items. Bookworm stores knowledge and information. If it is destroyed, it explodes into a flash of harmless white light. Injecting primeval essence turns it into a flash of white light that enters the forehead, between the eyebrows, and plants the stored information as content the user has memorised. It is precious and as rare as the Liquor worm, with demand and almost no supply once one appears. In Tong Ou shop Fang Yuan browses two copies lent by the elderly clerk, then returns them.",
        "chapters": [
          261
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
